menu "System Errors Options"
    config SYS_ERRORS_BUF_SIZE
        int "Error Pool Buffer Size (bytes)"
        default 1024
        range 128 8192
        help
          Total size of the bounded error node allocator's backing buffer.

    config SYS_ERRORS_BLOCK_SIZE
        int "Error Pool Block Size (bytes)"
        default 32
        range 8 256
        help
          Allocation granularity of the error node pool. SYS_ERRORS_BUF_SIZE
          must be evenly divisible by this value.

    config SYS_ERRORS_LOG_LINE_MAX
        int "Log Line Stack Buffer Size (bytes)"
        default 512
        range 64 4096
        help
          Stack buffer size the log hook renders one line into.

    config SYS_ERRORS_MAX_DOMAIN_HOOKS
        int "Maximum Domain Fault Hooks"
        default 8
        range 1 32
        help
          Slots for SE_register_domain_hook() (one per module domain that
          has containment logic for its own critical errors).

    config SYS_ERRORS_LOG_QUEUE_LEN
        int "Error Log Queue Length (chains)"
        default 4
        range 1 16
        help
          Error chains waiting for the log task. A waiting chain keeps its
          pool nodes, so keep this well under the pool's 32 blocks. When the
          queue is full a chain is dropped and counted; the count is logged.

    config SYS_ERRORS_REPEAT_WINDOW_MS
        int "Repeated Error Window (ms)"
        default 2000
        range 0 60000
        help
          A chain identical to one logged less than this long ago (same tag
          and owner at every node) is counted instead of logged and sent.
          When the window ends, one line reports how many repeats were
          dropped. Responses still run for every occurrence. 0 disables it.

    config SYS_ERRORS_REPEAT_SLOTS
        int "Repeated Error Slots"
        default 4
        range 1 16
        help
          How many different recent chains are tracked for repeat
          suppression.

    config SYS_ERRORS_LOG_TASK_STACK_SIZE
        int "Error Log Task Stack Size (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 2048 16384
        help
          The log task formats chains (two SYS_ERRORS_LOG_LINE_MAX buffers)
          and encodes packets (SYS_ERRORS_PACKET_MAX) on its own stack, so
          tasks that raise errors don't need that stack.

    config SYS_ERRORS_LOG_TASK_PRIO
        int "Error Log Task Priority"
        default 2
        range 1 24
        help
          Low on purpose: responses to errors run synchronously in the task
          that raised them; only logging and telemetry wait for this task.

    config SYS_ERRORS_PACKET_MAX
        int "Error Packet Buffer Size (bytes)"
        default 512
        range 64 4096
        help
          Compile-time ceiling for binary error packet buffer.
endmenu
